{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.88,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C2", "U1"],
      "pins": ["C2.1", "C2.2", "U1.2"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "GND"],
      "observed": "The LM1117-5.0 output is connected to C2, a 100 nF capacitor from +5V to GND; no larger output capacitor is shown.",
      "expected": "The LM1117 requires an appropriately sized output capacitor for stability; 100 nF alone is not an adequate substitute for the usual several-microfarad output capacitor.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C2\") (value \"100nF\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C2\") (pin \"1\")) ... (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"VO\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C2\") (pin \"2\")) ... (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"GND\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The regulator may oscillate or have poor transient response, making the +5V rail unstable and potentially disrupting the controller.",
      "confidence": 0.91
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U2", "U3"],
      "pins": ["U2.5", "U3.5", "U2.6", "U3.6", "U2.7", "U3.7"],
      "nets": ["SDA", "PWM", "SCK"],
      "observed": "The ATtiny45 (U2) and ATtiny13 (U3) have corresponding GPIO pins directly connected on the same signal nets, and both are also connected to the same +5V, GND, and reset nets.",
      "expected": "Only one MCU should be populated on these shared nets, or the MCU interfaces should be isolated. Two fitted MCUs can drive the same signals simultaneously.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"10\") (name \"PWM\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"PB1\")) ... (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"PB1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"12\") (name \"SCK\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"PB2\")) ... (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"PB2\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"13\") (name \"SDA\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"AREF/PB0\")) ... (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PB0\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If both listed MCUs are assembled and firmware configures shared pins differently, their outputs can contend, corrupt signals, or damage an MCU. The shared pinout may indicate an intended alternate-population option, but no exclusion or assembly instruction is present in the supplied files.",
      "confidence": 0.76
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The regulator output has only a 100 nF capacitor, which is inadequate for LM1117 stability. The netlist also places two MCUs on shared GPIO nets, creating a contention risk if both are populated."
}

